batch ast)\n1784:   Over a durable store the code index is not the session's to drop: the\n1785:   new indexer continues the old one's log, entity allocation, and\n1786:   published manifest (`yin.repl.index/carry-over`), so a rebuild never\n1793:                               (:index-store state)\n1795:           (store/durable? (:index-store state))\n1796:           (update :indexer index/carry-over (:indexer state)))\n1853:                   (if (store/durable? (:index-store state))\n1854:                     \" (VM store cleared; durable code index kept)\"\n2125:   to its lambda's root address (yin.vm.macro.md §10.1).  `:index` is the\n2126:   code indexer's `yin.repl.index/status`: whether every committed program\n2127:   is published, whether a gap lost the indexer, and its last failure.\n2128:   `:ast-index` is the AST indexer's `yin.repl.ast-index/status`: the sizes\n2154:   :index (index/status (:indexer state))\n2155:   :ast-index (ast-index/status (:ast-indexer state))\n262:(defn- blen\n305:  (span-key bs 0 (blen bs)))\n311:  (let [n (blen a)]\n312:    (and (= n (blen b))\n1126:                               (wire/byte-string (copy-range x 0 (blen x))))\n1139:(defn encode\n1159:  (copy-range bs 0 (blen bs)))\n1162:(defn encoded-compare\n1171:        la (blen ea)\n1172:        lb (blen eb)]\n1186:  (when (> (+ pos n) (blen bs))\n1307:                      (let [n (reduce + (map blen chunks))\n1313:                                                      off (+ off (blen c)) c)\n1317:                                  (+ off (blen c)))\n1449:      (if (and (= :bytes (:kind p)) (= 8 (blen b)))\n1495:                  (let [mag (span-big (:value p) 0 (blen (:value p)))]\n1544:  (when (zero? (blen bs))\n1547:    (when (not= pos (blen bs))\n1548:      (refuse :trailing-data (str (- (blen bs) pos) \" bytes after the item\")))\n39:(defn app\n64:(defn then\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
